{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on `b80ff35a`: yes to (a), (b) and (c). Add step 1 to the C4\nhead.\n\n- (a) The unit control in Node replaces the paired control. It pins\n  the wrapper: an `abort` that throws the workerd error prints one\n  line. Say in the test name what it proves, the wrapper, and what\n  it does not prove, the condition in workerd.\n- (b) The C4 gate is the Native witness. If it prints no line, that\n  is one gate with no crossing, and it is no proof that the guard\n  sees a real one. Then keep step 3 back until a gate prints a line\n  or a run shows the guard on a real crossing.\n- (c) Accepted as an inference from source, and labelled so in the\n  note.\n\nYour three runs are a useful fact for the note: a limit of 1 ms\nalone loses no timeout. The loss needs the timer to fire in the\nI/O context of another object.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}